  "zh": "素面地板的家：預設的家，地板沒有木紋（對照用）",
  "doc": "default_home with a plain floor (owner decision D1, 2026-09-27: the duck learns the floor from ground it walked without contact; this home is the comparison without plank seams). Generated from default_home.json by the phase-3 gates' make_plain_home.py (measurement records, not in the repo): everything but the floor's look is default_home's. The simulator page's room (duck3d.js buildRoom / buildNest, phase 0) made physical, in the page's own coordinates: world (x, y, z) = three.js (x, -z, y). Walls centred on Duck Core's ROOM_HALF_MM (engine.py), so the plan and the physics agree on the walls; all four walls are physical (the page fades the two between the camera and the duck, owner decision B4). The sofa stands on 9 cm legs (a 7 cm ball rolls under, the duck does not fit; curiosity spec 4.2). The rug is drawn and seen, not felt (visual only). The charging place is a robot-vacuum-style dock with its back on the middle of the south wall, facing into the room (owner decision 2026-09-27; duckmind.world.dock; the variants forward / backin pick how the duck docks — backin, turning round on the dock's right, is the default since 2026-09-28 —, open_nest brings back phase 2's open nest at the origin for comparison). Duck Core's frame stays the room (frame: room, the identity), so its imagined walls are these walls; a nest duck still believes its nest is at its origin (0, 0), the middle of the room, until phase 5 teaches it where the dock really is: the page shows both. A duck without a nest (no_nest, e.g. 蛋黃) lives on the mat at the origin. Units: mm, mrad, g; pos_mm = footprint centre and lowest point.",
